# ============================================================================
# Whitelist-style .gitignore for nearlink-E573H-USBDC
#
# Rule: nothing is tracked unless explicitly allowlisted below.
#   "*"        ignore every file and directory by default
#   "!*/"      re-open every directory so git can descend into it
#   "!pattern" allowlist specific names / file types
#
# The vendor SDK (ws73_sdk_linux_WS73_1.10.110) ships prebuilt binaries and
# build output; we commit only what this project actually needs (sources,
# docs, scripts, configs) and let the rest stay out of the tree.
#
#   stage something regardless of the rules:  git add -f <path>
#   find out why a file is ignored:           git check-ignore -v <path>
#   dry-run what would be tracked:            git status --short --ignored
# ============================================================================

# 1) Ignore everything by default
*

# 2) Allow directory traversal (required for the allowlist rules below)
!*/

# 3) Project metadata
!.gitignore
!LICENSE
!README*
!NOTICE*
!AUTHORS*
!CHANGELOG*
!COPYING*

# 4) Build & orchestration
!Makefile
!makefile
!*.mk
!CMakeLists.txt
!*.cmake
!Kconfig
!*.config
!*.sh
!*.py
!*.pl
!*.rb

# 5) Source code
!*.c
!*.h
!*.S
!*.s
!*.asm
!*.rs
!*.go
!*.java
!*.cpp
!*.cc
!*.cxx
!*.hpp
!*.ts
!*.js
!*.lua
!Kconfig
!Kconfig.*

# 6) Docs, data, configs
!*.md
!*.txt
!*.rst
!*.adoc
!*.csv
!*.xml
!*.json
!*.yaml
!*.yml
!*.ini
!*.cfg
!*.conf
!*.dts
!*.dtsi
!*.dtso
!*.map
!*.patch
!*.diff
!*.lds

# 7) Never tracked: archives, binaries, images, build output.
#    (These are simply NOT allowlisted above; explicit rules for clarity.)
*.zip
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.gz
*.bz2
*.xz
*.7z
*.rar
*.ko
*.o
*.a
*.so
*.so.*
*.elf
*.bin
*.img
*.fw
*.lib
*.exe
